#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1267 expect=noViolation domain=TA
#note "FRESH. Predicted SILENT: the authored pattern /^(-?[1-9]\\d*|0)$/ admits a bare 0 through its second alternation branch and a NEGATIVE integer through the optional sign, so neither row matches the negated leaf. That is over-permissive against the sheet's notion of a PLANNED ORDER of an element within an arm - see finding SD1267-F1 - but it is what the rule says, and this fixture encodes the rule as shipped, GREEN, not a D9 red. If either row FIRES it is a rendering question and therefore a stage-R classification - escalate, do not rewrite."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TA class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Arms"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col TAETORD type=Num  label="Planned Order of Element within Arm"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col EPOCH   type=Char label="Epoch"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TA | A | Placebo | 0  | SCRN | SCREENING
CDISCPILOT01 | TA | A | Placebo | -3 | TRT  | TREATMENT
